# T-E3-017 — Secret custody and rotation rules

1. objective: Define server-only secret custody and a rotation procedure.
2. outcome-link: FL3.3.2/F3.3.2/C3.3 — privileged material remains segregated from clients and ordinary AI.
3. preconditions + completed dependencies: T-E3-016 DONE for isolated defense via owner-accepted PR #22; hosted/privileged activation remains HELD. T-E3-001-R1 REVIEW.
4. mandatory reads: ADR-002 Option A/Decisions 1 and 6; ADR-006 Decision 11; TASK_INDEX/DEPENDENCY_GRAPH; MODULE_BOUNDARIES; TASK_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL/DEC-0068/0069; AI scope/defense/reversibility profiles; current maintenance configuration and dated official Supabase key/signing guidance.
5. allowed paths: vault/PROFILES/secret-custody-rotation.md, this pack, vault/REGISTRY/T-E3-017.md, vault/EVIDENCE/E-DEV-021.md, E3 manifest reference and generated registry/routing indexes.
6. forbidden areas: Runtime/tests/schemas/workflows, hosted tools/keys/passwords/roles/sessions, credential retrieval/rotation/revocation, deployments, secrets-store/provider choices, purchases, numeric limits/schedules and compatibility procedure implementation.
7. expected artifact changes: Credential/custodian rules, non-secret custody record, planned rotation steps, emergency/partial/recovery procedure, later closure proof and bounded task/evidence records.
8. acceptance + negative cases: Server-only secrets; rotation procedure. No client/AI privileged material, current product authority preserved; replacement/retirement/session/connection/cache/URL distinctions, cached maintenance config, wrong environment, compromise/no unsafe rollback, provider outage/no-owner-debug addressed. All live custody/rotation proof stays HELD.
9. validation / architecture / integration checks: Manual source/current-code/negative-case coverage; all 11 E10 checks; regenerate indexes; diff --check; exact-head applicable CI; independent gpt-6-luna max T3 review and owner acceptance. No new executable tests for document-only rules.
10. migration / rollback needs: None in this task; reviewed amendments only. Later execution has target-specific dry run, protected custody, revocation proof and safe rollback; never reactivate compromised/revoked access or lower floors.
11. responsive / accessibility rules: N/A; no UI. Owner summaries state outcome/risk/cost/reversibility plainly and do not delegate debugging.
12. evidence + handoff format: E-DEV-021 records normalized profile digest, coverage, actual E10/exact-head CI, independent model/context/head/verdict/findings and explicit owner acceptance; regression suites do not prove live rotation.
13. graph-update records: T-E3-017 REVIEW and E-DEV-021 plus generated indexes; preserve physical HELD/T-E3-001-R1 REVIEW; T-E3-018 and actual rotation/deployment remain separate.
14. escalation rules: Missing custody/consumer/revocation or compromised access holds capability; separately scoped privileged execution requires technical actor, independent T3 review and explicit owner acceptance. No standing administrative grant follows from document approval.

